Error [E0031]: Jet doesn't use `unsafe` to call Rust crates
  --> tests/ui/unsafe_extern_rust_teaching.jet:1:1
    |
  1 | unsafe extern rust "demo@1" {
    | ^^^^^^
 Why: foreign Rust functions live in whole `extern rust` blocks — callers never write `unsafe`
 Fix: write: extern rust "crate@version" { fn name(...) T = "rust::path"; }
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0031

Error [E0070]: this uses a retired arrow spelling
  --> tests/ui/unsafe_extern_rust_teaching.jet:2:17
    |
  2 |     fn answer() => Int :: "demo::answer"
    |                 ^^
 Why: callables, arms, and lambdas use one arrow: `->`
 Fix: replace `:>` or `=>` with `->`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0070

Error [E0068]: This callable uses the retired result-arrow shape.
  --> tests/ui/unsafe_extern_rust_teaching.jet:2:17
    |
  2 |     fn answer() => Int :: "demo::answer"
    |                 ^^
 Why: a return type sits after the parameter list, and `->` introduces the body; an effect ceiling follows the return type
 Fix: write `fn name(...) Type -> body`, or `fn name(...) Type -[Effects]> { … }`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0068

Error [E0003]: expected `=` before the Rust path, found `::`
  --> tests/ui/unsafe_extern_rust_teaching.jet:2:24
    |
  2 |     fn answer() => Int :: "demo::answer"
    |                        ^^
 Why: the structure here isn't what the compiler expected
 Fix: use `=` before the Rust path
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0003
